    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Please see Crystal-Ornelas et al. (In Revision) for details on how each reporting format crosswalk was constructed.\nIn general, each team developing the 11 ESS-DIVE (meta)data reporting formats followed a community centric approach to developing the data reporting formats. We note there are only 10 crosswalks because the model data archiving guidelines are such that there was no terminology to crosswalk with other existing data standards. The goal of creating a crosswalk for each reporting format was to ensure terminology used throughout the formats, as much as possible, included or built from terms used in other existing data standards and data resources. The crosswalks can be used to show how terms used in the ESS-DIVE reporting formats are related to terms used in other standards."
    ],
